Quoting  Moonsilence  <newsNO@JUNKmoonsilence.de>:
>What is the difference between MC and MR? I haven't been able to 
>understand from reading about it in "Maniac's Ascension Guide".

MR is a binary property; you either have it or you don't. It prevents such
effects as polytraps, teletraps, death rays and the touch of death
affecting you; as such, it is nigh-impossible to do without it in the late
game. MR is provided only by gray dragon scale mail, the cloak of magic
resistance, Magicbane, and certain Quest artifacts.

MC is a property of armour (only) which comes in 3 levels from 0 to 3,
with only the highest level on any piece of armour counting (there is no
additive effect). It blocks a variety of annoyances such as lycanthrophy,
item destruction from shocking attacks, level draining etc, but even MC3
is not completely effective. It is certainly possible to ascend with MC2;
theoretically it ought to be so with MC1 or MC0, but in practice there's
no compelling late-game reason not to have at least MC2. Many pieces of
armour provide MC so you would have to check a spoiler to see exactly
which.

